  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is LocalStorage?</h2>
    <p><b>LocalStorage = A Small Storage Box Inside Your Browser.</b> You can save data there, and it stays even after you refresh the page, close the tab, or restart the browser.</p>
    <p>Example: You type your name on a website, refresh the page, and your name is still there. That is LocalStorage. Without LocalStorage, all data is lost on refresh. With LocalStorage, data is saved forever until you delete it.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Real Life Example:</b> YouTube remembers your dark mode. Facebook remembers you are logged in. Shopping sites remember your cart. All of these use LocalStorage or similar storage.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - My Notes - Saved Forever</h2>
    <p>Add a note, then refresh the page. Your note will still be there - That is LocalStorage:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <h3 style="margin:0">📝 My Notes - Saved in LocalStorage</h3>
      <p style="color:#64748b;font-size:13px">Try: Add note - Refresh page - Note is still here ✅</p>
      <input class="demo-input" id="noteInput" type="text" placeholder="Type a note - e.g. Buy milk">
      <button class="btn btn-js" onclick="saveNote()">Save Note 💾</button>
      <button class="btn" onclick="clearNotes()">Clear All 🧹</button>
      <div id="notesList" style="margin-top:12px"></div>
      <p id="notesCount" style="color:#64748b;font-size:13px">Total Notes: 0</p>
    </div>
    <h2>3. 4 Main Commands - Full Table</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Command</th><th>What It Does</th><th>Example</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>setItem(key, value)</b></td><td>Save data</td><td>localStorage.setItem("name", "Ali")</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>getItem(key)</b></td><td>Read data</td><td>localStorage.getItem("name") - Returns "Ali"</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>removeItem(key)</b></td><td>Delete one item</td><td>localStorage.removeItem("name")</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>clear()</b></td><td>Delete everything</td><td>localStorage.clear()</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// SAVE</span><br>
<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("name", "Ali");</span><br>
<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("city", "Lahore");</span><br>
<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("age", "20");</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// READ</span><br>
<span class="text">let myName = localStorage.getItem("name");</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(myName); // "Ali"</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// DELETE ONE</span><br>
<span class="text">localStorage.removeItem("city");</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// DELETE ALL</span><br>
<span class="text">localStorage.clear();</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>4. Important Rule - Only Strings!</h2>
    <p>LocalStorage can only save <b>strings</b> (text). If you try to save a number, it becomes a string. If you try to save an array or object, it becomes <code>"[object Object]"</code> - Broken!</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("age", 20);</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(typeof localStorage.getItem("age")); // "string" - Not number!</span><br><br>
<span class="text">let user = { name: "Ali", age: 20 };</span><br>
<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("user", user); // ❌ WRONG</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(localStorage.getItem("user")); // "[object Object]" - Broken!</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>5. Solution - JSON.stringify and JSON.parse</h2>
    <p>To save an object or array, first convert it to a JSON string with <code>JSON.stringify()</code>. When you read it back, convert it to object again with <code>JSON.parse()</code>.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// SAVE OBJECT - Correct Way</span><br>
<span class="text">let user = { name: "Ali", age: 20, city: "Lahore" };</span><br>
<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("user", JSON.stringify(user));</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(localStorage.getItem("user")); // '{"name":"Ali","age":20,"city":"Lahore"}' - A string</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// READ OBJECT - Convert back</span><br>
<span class="text">let saved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("user"));</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(saved.name); // "Ali"</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// SAVE ARRAY - Same way</span><br>
<span class="text">let todos = ["Buy milk", "Study JS", "Walk"];</span><br>
<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("todos", JSON.stringify(todos));</span><br>
<span class="text">let savedTodos = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("todos"));</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(savedTodos[0]); // "Buy milk"</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Memory Trick:</b> <b>stringify</b> = Object to String (Save). <b>parse</b> = String to Object (Read). You <b>stringify</b> before <b>setItem</b>, and <b>parse</b> after <b>getItem</b>.</div>
    <h2>6. Check If Data Exists</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let savedName = localStorage.getItem("name");</span><br><br>
<span class="text">if (savedName === null) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">console.log("No data saved yet - First time user");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("name", "Guest");</span><br>
<span class="text">} else {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">console.log("Welcome back, " + savedName);</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <p>If the key does not exist, <code>getItem()</code> returns <code>null</code>. Always check for null before using the data.</p>
    <h2>7. Complete Example - Dark Mode That Remembers</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;body</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"page"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h1&gt;</span><span class="text">My Website</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"toggleTheme()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Toggle Theme 🌙</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// On page load - Read saved theme</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let savedTheme = localStorage.getItem("theme");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (savedTheme === "dark") {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("page").style.backgroundColor = "#0f172a";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("page").style.color = "white";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function toggleTheme() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let current = localStorage.getItem("theme");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (current === "dark") {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("theme", "light");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">location.reload(); // Refresh to apply</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">} else {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("theme", "dark");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">location.reload();</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>8. LocalStorage vs SessionStorage</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Feature</th><th>LocalStorage</th><th>SessionStorage</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Stays after refresh?</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Stays after closing tab?</td><td>Yes - Forever</td><td>No - Deleted when tab closes</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Use for</td><td>Theme, Name, Cart, Notes</td><td>One-time login, Temporary data</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p>Code is same, only name changes: <code>sessionStorage.setItem("name", "Ali")</code></p>
    <h2>9. Homework</h2>
    <p>In Playground, build this:</p>
    <p>1. Name Saver - Input + Save button. Save name in LocalStorage. On page load, show "Welcome back, [name]" if name exists<br>2. Counter - Button adds +1, counter value saved in LocalStorage. Refresh page, counter stays same<br>3. Theme Saver - Dark/Light button, save theme in LocalStorage like example above</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> LocalStorage = Browser storage, stays after refresh | setItem(key, value) = Save | getItem(key) = Read, returns null if not found | removeItem(key) = Delete one | clear() = Delete all | Only strings - Use JSON.stringify to save object/array, JSON.parse to read back | SessionStorage = Same but deleted when tab closes</div>
