        <form id="quizForm">
          <div class="question"><b>Q1. What is LocalStorage?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="a"> Browser storage - Data stays even after refresh</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="b"> A color</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="c"> A loop</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="d"> A database on server</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q2. How to save data?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="a"> localStorage.setItem("name", "Ali")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="b"> localStorage.save("name", "Ali")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="c"> localStorage.add("name", "Ali")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="d"> localStorage.put("name", "Ali")</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q3. How to read data?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="a"> localStorage.getItem("name")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="b"> localStorage.read("name")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="c"> localStorage.get("name")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="d"> localStorage.show("name")</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q4. What does getItem return if key does not exist?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="a"> null</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="b"> 0</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="c"> "" - Empty string</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="d"> Error</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q5. How to delete one item?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="a"> localStorage.removeItem("name")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="b"> localStorage.delete("name")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="c"> localStorage.clear("name")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="d"> localStorage.remove("name")</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q6. How to delete everything?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="a"> localStorage.clear()</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="b"> localStorage.removeAll()</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="c"> localStorage.deleteAll()</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="d"> localStorage.empty()</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q7. What can LocalStorage save directly?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="a"> Only strings (text)</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="b"> Objects directly</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="c"> Arrays directly</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="d"> Functions</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q8. How to save an object correctly?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="a"> localStorage.setItem("user", JSON.stringify(user))</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="b"> localStorage.setItem("user", user)</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="c"> localStorage.setItem("user", JSON.parse(user))</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="d"> localStorage.setItem(user)</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q9. How to read an object back?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="a"> JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("user"))</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="b"> JSON.stringify(localStorage.getItem("user"))</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="c"> localStorage.getItem("user") only</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="d"> JSON.parse("user")</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q10. LocalStorage vs SessionStorage?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="a"> LocalStorage stays forever, SessionStorage deletes when tab closes</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="b"> Both delete on refresh</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="c"> SessionStorage stays forever</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="d"> Both are same</label></div>
          <button type="button" class="btn" onclick="checkTest(false)">Submit Test - Check Result</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-next" onclick="resetTest()">Try Again</button>
        </form>
